{
  "description": "What each shared IFC fixture must import as, in both IFC importers (see make_fixtures.py). Segments are [start, end] in world metres; width and height_limit_m are the profile's; regions give the count, total area (to 2%: curves are drawn with chords) and [min x, max x, min y, max y] of a section's regions; materials are the sorted material ids of the profile's layers or regions. Optional: segment_types (line or arc, in order), arc_radius (the distance of an arc's start, mid and end from the origin), either_direction (the path may run the other way), layers (the band names, left to right), layer_thicknesses, origin_x (the profile's), closed (the path is a loop), cap_start, cap_end, cap_end_angle_deg, openings (path_position, width_m, height_m, sill_height_m of each, along the path), and per fixture slabs (outline points in order, from any start, either way round; thickness_m, elevation_m, material_id).",
